{"id":"hushai","name":"Hushai","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:hushai"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hushai","text":"Quick, “the Archite,” “the king’s friend” (1 Chr. 27:33). When David fled from Jerusalem, on account of the rebellion of Absalom, and had reached the summit of Olivet, he there met Hushai, whom he sent back to Jerusalem for the purpose of counteracting the influence of Ahithophel, who had joined the ranks of Absalom (2 Sam. 15:32, 37; 16:16-18). It was by his advice that Absalom refrained from immediately pursuing after David. By this delay the cause of Absalom was ruined, for it gave David time to muster his forces."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2365","lemma":"חוּשַׁי","xlit":"Chûwshay","gloss":"Chushai, an Israelite","kjv":"Hushai","count":6,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H53","lemma":"אֲבִישָׁלוֹם","xlit":"ʼĂbîyshâlôwm","gloss":"Abshalom, a son of David","kjv":"Abishalom, Absalom","count":5,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H757","lemma":"אַרְכִּי","xlit":"ʼArkîy","gloss":"an Arkite or native of Erek","kjv":"Archi, Archite","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H7463","lemma":"רֵעֶה","xlit":"rêʻeh","gloss":"a companion","kjv":"friend","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H302","lemma":"אֲחִיתֹפֶל","xlit":"ʼĂchîythôphel","gloss":"Achithophel, an Israelite","kjv":"Ahithophel","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H54","lemma":"אֶבְיָתָר","xlit":"ʼEbyâthâr","gloss":"Ebjathar, an Israelite","kjv":"Abiathar","count":2,"share":0.17}],"verses":["2Sam.15.32","2Sam.15.37","2Sam.16.16","2Sam.16.17","2Sam.16.18","1Chr.27.33","2Sam.15.33","2Sam.15.34","2Sam.15.35","2Sam.15.36","2Sam.16.19","2Sam.17.0"],"related":[{"id":"zadok","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.093,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"diplomacy","type":"cooccur","shared":10,"jaccard":0.05,"why":"10 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"strategy","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.046,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"friendship","type":"coo